<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Creek Mechanical is built by a working mechanical engineer, out of frustration with free CAD tools that require uploading proprietary files to a server."
>
  <article class="prose wrap">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Creek Mechanical is built by a working mechanical engineer. Most free
      CAD conversion and analysis tools on the web require uploading your
      file to someone else's server — a non-starter for anyone working under
      an NDA, or who simply doesn't want proprietary geometry leaving their
      machine. This site exists to fix that: every tool runs entirely in
      your browser, using WebAssembly, so nothing you open is ever
      transmitted anywhere.
    </p>
    <p>
      The tools here are free because they're useful, and because they're a
      genuine demonstration of the kind of work available through
      <a href="/services/">freelance engineering services</a>. If a tool
      surfaces a problem with your file, that's usually a problem we can fix
      for you directly.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
